{"abstract":"This paper critically examines the machine learning (ML) modeling of humans in three case studies of well-being technologies. Through a critical technical approach, it examines how these apps were experienced in daily life (technology in use) to surface breakdowns and to identify the assumptions about the “human” body entrenched in the ML models (technology design). To address these issues, this paper applies agential realism to decenter foundational assumptions, such as body regularity and health/illness binaries, and speculates more inclusive design and ML modeling paths that acknowledge irregularity, human-system entanglements, and uncertain transitions. This work is among the first to explore the implications of decentering theories in computational modeling of human bodies and well-being, offering insights for more inclusive technologies and speculations toward posthuman-centered ML modeling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhu, Jichen","Sanches, Pedro","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","van der Maden, Willem","Kaklopoulou, Irene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808913"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Agential realism","Decentering","Diffraction","Well being"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the centers and margins of modeling humans in well being technologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713940","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808913","identifier":[{"id":"105005712509","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6340b37e-db29-4950-99d9-e79c2f96d4a4"],"keyword":["Agential Realism","Decentering","Diffraction","Machine Learning Modeling","Well-being"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2699132873982139CD21194131A7BEB7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713940","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Willem","key":"vandermadenpau","last":"van der Maden","locid":"1ee9fda3-cb4e-4c06-82b1-7e248c20a700","name":"van der Maden, Willem","orcid":"0000-0003-0245-1633","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"kaklopouloupau","last":"Kaklopoulou","name":"Kaklopoulou, Irene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3706598.3713940","eisbn":["9798400713941"],"pages":"1-16","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2025 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005712509"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6340b37e-db29-4950-99d9-e79c2f96d4a4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Centers and Margins of Modeling Humans in Well-being Technologies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808913","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Most users interact with explainable AI (XAI) systems through an interface. Despite the growing assemblage of human-centered XAI literature, there is still limited research that investigates how explanations are presented in interfaces. With this preliminary study, we propose a novel approach to analyze the content and interactions of explainable interfaces by mapping UI elements and interactions to the type of explanation they convey. Based on analysis of 28 explainable interfaces, we offer initial findings of how various interaction concepts and UI elements are used to provide different explanations.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Meyer, Louie Søs","Zhu, Jichen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776455"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Explanation types","human centered XAI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"slide to explore what if an analysis of explainable interfaces","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206566341","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776455","identifier":[{"id":"85206566341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e8c86569-6691-40c8-8ebd-b350b2457a54"],"keyword":["explainable AI interfaces","explanation types","human-centered XAI","interaction concepts","user interface elements"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D63386A1730B4404A5655221614F2046"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louie Søs","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"b55a7155-5e64-4230-b7da-94f7872e9742","name":"Meyer, Louie Søs","orcid":"0009-0008-7490-3049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685416","journal":"Proceedings of NordiCHI","pages":"1-6","paperid":"2","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of NordiCHI"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206566341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8c86569-6691-40c8-8ebd-b350b2457a54"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Slide to Explore 'What If': An Analysis of Explainable Interfaces","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776455","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This workshop explores the transformative potential of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) in design research. GenAI, capable of creating new content such as images, text, music, video, and code, raises important questions about authorship, agency, and design practice. Inspired by Roland Barthes' \"The Death of the Author,\"this workshop examines how GenAI reshapes design research roles and methods. Key topics include best practices, ethical considerations, knowledge generation, and collaboration patterns between human and AI creatives. Building on themes identified in the successful DIS 2023 workshop, this 2-day event invites designers and researchers to present completed projects, works-in-progress, and theoretical provocations. The structure allows time for both presentations and in-depth discussions, aiming to develop an online resource library and a collaborative publication. The workshop seeks to advance the discourse on GenAI, addressing its challenges and opportunities in design research.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Van Der Maden, Willem","Van Beek, Evert","Halperin, Brett A.","Jääskeläinen, Petra","Kang, Eunsu","Kun, Peter","Lomas, James Derek","Merritt, Timothy","Lindley, Joseph","Muller, Michael","Nicenboim, Iohanna","Zhu, Jichen","van der Burg, Vera"],"cuid":["S02-088.22-803632"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Van Der Maden, Willem"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Delft University of Technology","IBM","IBM Research","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Lancaster University","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Computational Creativity","Creative practices","Design research","Generative artificial intelligence"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"death of the design researcher creating knowledge resources for designers using generative ai","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3658398","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.22-803632","identifier":[{"id":"85198903016","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2401a2f0-09d2-4f14-ab3f-9d8f4710e95c","itu-9e885c49-7cff-4d78-b330-271757e69dc6"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","computational creativity","creative practices","design research","generative artifcial intelligence","generative artificial intelligence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-75785C455AD10E2B6FC74001F2114BF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/752689253/3656156.3658398.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3658398","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","ke